COMMENT     The assembly dhQueRobu3.1 is based on 37x PacBio data, 10X Genomics
            Chromium data, and Arima Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of
            Life Project (https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly
            process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio
            assembly generation with Hifiasm, retained haplotig separation with
            purge_dups, short-read polishing using FreeBayes-called variants
            from 10X Genomics Chromium reads aligned with LongRanger, and Hi-C
            based scaffolding with SALSA2. The mitochondrial and chloroplast
            genomes were assembled with MBG from PacBio HiFi reads mapping to
            related genomes. A representative circular sequence was selected
            for each from the graph based on read coverage. Finally, the
            assembly was analysed and manually improved using gEVAL.
            Chromosome-scale scaffolds are named by synteny based on PMID:
            27013549.
